`mode: 'replace'` is documented in `DatasetMode` as "Delete ALL records in object then insert", but the implementation just inserts new records and never clears existing data. This makes `replace` behave the same as `insert` and breaks idempotent seed usage. Consider performing a `delete`/truncate for the target object before inserting (ideally once per dataset, not per record), or rejecting `replace` with an explicit error if full-table replace isn't supported here.
```suggestion
        // Replace mode is defined as "delete ALL records in object then insert".
        // This seed loader does not implement the required delete-all behavior,
        // so we reject this mode explicitly to avoid non-idempotent inserts.
        throw new Error(
          `Seed loader does not implement 'replace' mode (delete-all-then-insert) for object '${objectName}'.`,
        );
```

Deferred updates key the record to update using `recordExternalId: String(record[externalId] ?? '')`. If the record is missing the externalId field (allowed by current behavior/tests), this becomes an empty string and pass-2 will be unable to find `recordId` in `insertedRecords`, silently skipping the update without emitting an error. Consider storing the inserted record's internal id (returned by `writeRecord`) in the deferred update, or maintaining a per-dataset recordIndex → id map so pass-2 can always target the right record even when `externalId` is absent.
```suggestion
            const recordExternalIdValue = record[externalId];
            if (recordExternalIdValue === undefined || recordExternalIdValue === null || recordExternalIdValue === '') {
              // Cannot safely defer without a usable externalId to identify the record in pass 2
              const error: ReferenceResolutionError = {
                sourceObject: objectName,
                field: ref.field,
                targetObject: ref.targetObject,
                targetField: ref.targetField,
                attemptedValue: fieldValue,
                recordIndex: i,
                message: `Cannot defer reference for multi-pass load: ${objectName}.${ref.field} = '${fieldValue}' → record is missing externalId '${externalId}'`,
              };
              errors.push(error);
              allErrors.push(error);
            } else {
              // Defer to pass 2
              record[ref.field] = null;
              deferredUpdates.push({
                objectName,
                recordExternalId: String(recordExternalIdValue),
                field: ref.field,
                targetObject: ref.targetObject,
                targetField: ref.targetField,
                attemptedValue: fieldValue,
                recordIndex: i,
              });
              referencesDeferred++;
            }
```

`SeedLoaderConfig` includes `batchSize` and `transaction`, but `load()`/`loadDataset()` never read these values. This means callers can set them with no effect, and `transaction: true` currently provides no all-or-nothing semantics. Consider either implementing these options (e.g., chunking by `batchSize`, using `engine.batch(..., { transaction: true })` when supported) or explicitly rejecting/ignoring them with a logged warning so behavior is unambiguous.
```suggestion

    // Warn for currently-unsupported config options so behavior is explicit
    if (config.batchSize !== undefined || config.transaction) {
      this.logger.warn('[SeedLoader] batchSize/transaction options are currently ignored by runtime implementation', {
        batchSize: config.batchSize,
        transaction: config.transaction,
      });
    }
```
